# No ADRs in public docs

ADRs live in `docs/decisions/` for agents and maintainers. Readers of `/docs`, npm READMEs, and generated type tables never see them.

TSDoc on public exports is public docs. AutoTypeTable prints it as-is.

## Do

- State the rule in the page (query-only, providers vs drivers)
- Link other `/docs` pages, `/security`, or https://db-sdk.dev

## Do not

- Write “See ADR 0003”, “ADR 0002”, or any ADR number
- Link `docs/decisions/*` or GitHub ADR blobs
- Use ADR numbers as the reader’s next step

```mdx
<!-- Bad -->
Hosted products keep their own `id`. See ADR 0003.

<!-- Good -->
Hosted products keep their own `id` and set `driver` to the underlying database.
```

```ts
/** Shared database implementation. See ADR 0003. */
// Bad — this text appears on /docs

/** Shared database implementation this provider reads through. */
// Good
```
